{
 "fps": 30,
 "totalFrames": 1731,
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "A glass flask shattered on a hard floor, and then it simply refused to fall apart.",
   "from": 0,
   "to": 133
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Paris, nineteen oh three: the lab of the chemist and artist \u00c9douard B\u00e9n\u00e9dictus.",
   "from": 137,
   "to": 277
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "He expected a mess of splinters. But the flask had cracked into a web, and kept its shape.",
   "from": 281,
   "to": 402
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Inside, it had held collodion, a liquid plastic, which dried into a clear film that held every shard.",
   "from": 406,
   "to": 574
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "He set it aside, and forgot all about it.",
   "from": 578,
   "to": 641
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Then Paris filled with motor cars, and the cars began to crash.",
   "from": 644,
   "to": 742
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "The story goes that he read about a crash where people were cut by flying glass.",
   "from": 746,
   "to": 853
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "speaker": "benedictus",
   "text": "That old flask, it held together!",
   "from": 856,
   "to": 905
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "And as the story is told, he worked all night on a new kind of glass.",
   "from": 908,
   "to": 1004
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "You see, he made a sandwich: glass, a thin layer of plastic, then glass again. When it breaks, the shards stick to the plastic.",
   "from": 1020,
   "to": 1204
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "He patented it in nineteen oh nine. But car makers were slow to want it.",
   "from": 1208,
   "to": 1338
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "So its first big job was in the First World War: the eyepieces of gas masks.",
   "from": 1342,
   "to": 1503
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Then it went into car windshields, and it is still there today.",
   "from": 1506,
   "to": 1610
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "So when a stone hits your windshield, it cracks like that flask, and holds.",
   "from": 1614,
   "to": 1707
  }
 ],
